  "worked_solution": "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=-4,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=4A\\operatorname{cos}\u20614x-4B\\operatorname{sin}\u20614x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=-4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4=4A\\,\u27f9\\,A=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\operatorname{sin}\u20614x+\\operatorname{cos}\u20614x.\n$$",
